    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe create audit line is emitted by `AuditOwnerCreated.service(...)`. It already logged `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate` and `membershipLevel`. I added `membershipNumber`, keeping the existing fields:\n\n`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`\n- Extended the log format with ` membershipNumber={}`.\n- Added a private `membershipNumber(owner)` helper that reproduces the exact format used by `OwnerMapper` for the DTO's `membershipNumber` field \u2014 `customerCode + \"-M\" + %02d(registrationDate.year % 100)` \u2014 so the audited value matches what the API returns (which is what the test asserts against).\n\nSample line now:\n```\nAUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-08-10 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\n## Tests\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes (Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).\n\nOne note: I mirrored the membership-number format by hand in the audit function because it lives as an inline expression in `OwnerMapper`, not a shared helper. If that format ever changes, both sites need updating \u2014 worth extracting into `MembershipLevel` (or a small helper) if you want a single source of truth.",
